{Opening moves not given but I (JS) am speculating they were as follows:} 1. e4
e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Qe2 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d6 9.
d4 Bg4 10. Rd1 Qc8 11. Bg5 Na5 12. Bc2 c5 13. dxc5 dxc5 {(To this point, the
moves given follow Keres-Turn, Tallinn 1943, hence my theory as to the opening
sequence - JS)} 14. Nbd2 Re8 15. h3 Bh5 16. Nf1 Nc4 17. b3 Na3 {[#]This is the
starting position given in CHESS...} 18. g4 $4 (18. Rac1 $11) 18... Bxg4 19.
hxg4 Nxc2 20. Bxf6 Bxf6 21. g5 Bd8 22. Rac1 Na3 {and Black won. Source (moves
18w-22b - the rest of the moves are speculation): Chess, Vol.28, No.422, 20
December 1962} 0-1

